														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3823555">
									

<p>I definitely understand where you're coming from. 3999 and other similarly-meta or similarly-personal skips are what drew me to this site - they are unabashedly an inspiration, and I could not reasonably hope to make as big a splash as 3999 did when it was first posted. Nor could I claim that this would exist without those articles.</p>
<p>However, I feel like there is room on this site for more experimental literature that delve into higher-concept topics: whether it be the difficulty of the creative process (a la 3999), issues surrounding the idea of the self/identity (like this one), the nature of fiction and its role in society (3211, 3500, and others), the inherent limitations of the Foundation's modus operandi (3005 comes to mind), and others. Just my two cents.</p>

							</div>

								
					
